<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar outflows at $2 mln Jan 8.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar outflows at $2 mln Jan 8.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-01-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $2 million deficit on Jan 8 in the commercial forex market, according to Central Bank data supplied to banks.</p>
<p>A banker with access to the figures said the central bank issued the following breakdown.</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON JANUARY 8</p>
<p>Exports: $161.9 million</p>
<p>Imports: $241 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $204 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $126.9 million</p>
<p>Deficit: $2 million</p>
<p>JANUARY DOLLAR FLOWS UP TO DATE</p>
<p>Exports: $959 million</p>
<p>Imports: $1.149 billion</p>
<p>Financial buy: $1.187 billion</p>
<p>Financial sell: $899 million</p>
<p>Net surplus: $98 million</p>
<p>Note: the figures were rounded off.</p>
<p>-- Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo newsroom, 55-11-2485418))</p>
</text>
